3.2 jsqr

  jsqr runs in the browser: it reads the learning kit's QR code
  (src/lib/learning/qrread.ts). Its licence, Apache License 2.0, is the
  package's node_modules/jsqr/LICENSE: the standard text, with the appendix's
  copyright line left as the unfilled template. The Apache License 2.0 text in
  public/mediapipe/LICENSE-mediapipe.txt is the same as jsqr's (only the
  brackets in the appendix template differ: jsqr's are braces, "{yyyy} {name
  of copyright owner}", and that file's are square brackets, "[yyyy] [name of
  copyright owner]"). That file also ends with a notice that applies to
  MediaPipe only (see section 1.3).

3.3 @google/genai

  Licence: Apache License 2.0. The package carries node_modules/@google/genai/
  LICENSE: the standard text, with the appendix's copyright line left as the
  unfilled template, and no NOTICE file. That text is the same as the Apache
  License 2.0 text at the top of public/mediapipe/LICENSE-mediapipe.txt, up to
  the end of the appendix (compared 2026-10-04: no difference but one blank
  line at the start of the package's file). The repo file goes on after that
  with a notice that applies to MediaPipe only (see 1.3); the package's file
  has nothing after the appendix. Both use square brackets in the appendix
  template ("[yyyy] [name of copyright owner]"); jsqr's uses braces (see 3.2).

3.4 drizzle-orm

  Licence: Apache License 2.0, as the "license" field in package.json and
  package-lock.json says. The package folder holds no LICENSE or NOTICE file,
  and its README states no licence (checked 2026-10-04), so there is no copy
  or copyright line of the package's own to point to. Its upstream licence file
  was not checked: Unconfirmed. The Apache License 2.0 text is in
  public/mediapipe/LICENSE-mediapipe.txt (standard text; the appendix template
